      "id": "poCxCGE6iPY",
      "title": "Glimpses along the Way   A Train Journey from Stewarton to Stranraer",
      "publishedAt": "2026-11-13T13:18:56Z",
      "durationSec": 212,
      "thumb": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/poCxCGE6iPY/mqdefault.jpg",
      "description": "The Girvan to Stranraer line is soon to be a 'one engine in steam' line with a single token issued at Girvan signal box. At present passing loops exist at Girvan, Kilkerran, Barrhill, Glenwhilly and Dunragit, with token exchanges at Glenwhilly and Dunragit. Barrhill is staffed with a signal box and the passing loop is in use. The points at Stranraer have been removed and therefore the second platform cannot be accessed and signalling is redundant.",
      "chapters": []
    },
    {
      "id": "OfEaFgBagFw",
      "title": "Hopton Heath railway station, Heart of Wales Line, Shropshire",
      "publishedAt": "2026-11-02T16:43:49Z",
      "durationSec": 146,
      "thumb": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/OfEaFgBagFw/mqdefault.jpg",
      "description": "Hopton Heath railway station lies on the Heart of Wales Line that tuns between Llanelli and Craven Arms. It is a request stop and has a single platform, the passing loop and signal box were removed in 1965. The station has 5/6 trains a day in each direction and two each way on Sundays.",
      "chapters": []
    },
    {
      "id": "KSRLt2kqjVI",
      "title": "Creating the 'Chapeltoun and Trewithen Railway' in 'T' Gauge",
      "publishedAt": "2026-10-18T18:11:09Z",
      "durationSec": 445,
      "thumb": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/KSRLt2kqjVI/mqdefault.jpg",
      "description": "Creating a 'Set of Memories' using 'T' Gauge track and 1:450 scale buildings, figures, trees, etc. The sites on the railway layout are mostly linked to places in Ayrshire, Nithsdale and a few are elsewhere in the UK. The layout is only 90cms by 30cms and it is transported in a folding case. The locomotives are powered by a controller with three AA batteries. Steam locomotives are not available.",
      "chapters": []
    },
    {
      "id": "KXq2SPPczr0",
      "title": "Balgray Railway Station, Neilston Branch",
      "publishedAt": "2026-10-05T15:27:07Z",
      "durationSec": 212,
      "thumb": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/KXq2SPPczr0/mqdefault.jpg",
      "description": "Balgray railway station was opened on the Neilston Branch on 27 September 2026 to serve the Barrhead area. The line used to continue through Uplawmoor and Kilwinning to Irvine and Ardrossan. The station to the east is Patterton and Neilston lies to the west. Trains arrive every 30 minutes and run through to Glasgow Central.",
      "chapters": []
    },
